  nonce: '5987'  # 5987
  data:  # 5987
    kind: work_item  # 5987
    title: "Guard the classified-yet-starved contradiction itself: five per-row fixes (INV-nular, WI-komun, INV-fugus, INV-dihun x2), each found by its symptom, and no check asserts that a module the classifier matched into is never reported starved"  # 5987
    status: todo_hard  # 5987
    priority: 3  # 5987
    parent:  # 5987
    tags:  # 5987
    - io_boundary  # 5987
    - verify_claims  # 5987
    - catalogue  # 5987
    isbefore: []  # 5987
    duplicate_of: []  # 5987
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 5987
    pr_ref:  # 5987
    description: "RESIDUAL of INV-dihun (satisfied on its filed instances by PR #1155). INV-dihun's statement is general: no module the classifier matched a call into may be reported by method_starved_modules in the same run. That was fixed FIVE times, one row at a time: INV-nular (rust File::open), WI-komun (JS console and friends), INV-fugus (python datetime), INV-dihun (JS process, python ctypes.cdll). Each instance was found by its symptom. Every row sweep since then has been limited by construction: INV-fugus's sweep resolved only CLASSES, which is how ctypes.cdll slipped past it.\n\nWHAT IS MISSING: a guard keyed on the CONTRADICTION rather than on rows. Options, not chosen:\n  (a) A test over the fixture corpus that runs each analyzer's fixtures through classify_call and method_starved_modules and asserts the intersection is empty.\n  (b) A runtime self-check inside compute_boundary_coverage: when a starved module has a classified edge in the same run, report it as an internal inconsistency rather than as blindness.\n(b) must NOT satisfy the module. Loosening the gate on \"any classified edge\" was refused for INV-fugus (test_a_METHOD_name_on_an_unstamped_edge_still_starves pins it).\nCorpus state at 10b8576108: 0 contradictions on 21 surveys (swift 4, scala 3, java 4, kotlin 1, objc 2, js 7). INV-zikab's axiom is the long-run cure; this guard is what catches the next row before a user does."  # 5987
    fields: {}  # 5987
- op: discuss  # 7c4d
  at: '2026-10-01T09:07:31Z'  # 7c4d
  by: agent  # 7c4d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7c4d
  clock: 2  # 7c4d
  nonce: 7c4d  # 7c4d
  message: "SIXTH INSTANCE, found by WI-zohuk (2026-10-01): javascript WebSocket / EventSource through the WI-dosuh handler-assignment edge. `ws.onmessage = h` emits javascript:WebSocket:0-0:onmessage with call_construct \"assignment\"; io-boundaries classifies it net_recv (WebSocket.onmessage), and method_starved_modules reports WebSocket starved in the same run, because \"assignment\" is not a member of the module's kind set {method} and onmessage is not a function-kind row. On a 5-line fixture (const ws = new WebSocket(u); ws.onmessage = function(ev){console.log(ev.data)}; plus an untyped sink.write(\"x\")) this flips all 7 generic claims from confirmed_with_caveats (arm A, construct withheld) to inconclusive (arm B, HEAD). On the measured corpus (vscode, lila, nestjs, nest, argo-cd) it fired 0 times: each emitting repo also has a method-stamped call on the same receiver type (es.close(), eventSource.close()), which satisfies route 1. Mechanism detail and repro are on WI-dapap (its remedy (2) names this exact cross-axis test). Option (a) of this item, run over a fixture with a handler assignment and no other call on the receiver, would have caught it."  # 7c4d
- op: discuss  # c23a
  at: '2026-10-01T21:37:41Z'  # c23a
  by: agent  # c23a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c23a
  clock: 3  # c23a
  nonce: c23a  # c23a
  message: "FROM WI-dapap (2026-10-01, branch jgstern-agent/fix/dapap-call-construct-allowlist, commit 425771854b, NOT merged). This bears on the sixth instance above and on a seventh, latent one.\n\n- The sixth instance is fixed on that branch at its mechanism, not at its row. method_starved_modules no longer tests call_construct for membership in the module's IoPrimitive.kind set. It translates the construct through call_constructs.reached_row_kind, which gives the ADR-0059 kind of the row the construct reaches. On WI-zohuk's fixture, dev gives 7/7 inconclusive (WebSocket starved) and the branch gives 7/7 confirmed_with_caveats, end to end through survey + verify-claims.\n- A seventh instance, with the same mechanism, is fixed by the same change: python construct 'protocol'. `for o in qs` emits django.db.models.__iter__; the classifier matches it against a method-kind row. On dev, a repo whose ONLY call into django.db.models is a for-loop over a QuerySet would report the module starved. This is pinned by test_a_python_protocol_edge_satisfies_the_orm_module, which goes red when the old test is restored. The corpus volume is 0: on a django survey with 660 protocol edges into the module, the starved list is identical before and after, because method-stamped ORM calls are also present.\n- This does NOT build this item's contradiction guard: neither option (a) nor (b) is implemented. The next row-level instance would still be found by its symptom."  # c23a
- op: discuss  # 5ad0
  at: '2026-10-25T23:58:43Z'  # 5ad0
  by: agent  # 5ad0
