  clock: 4  # 5ad0
  nonce: 5ad0  # 5ad0
  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 9245df71d6 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures, scratchpad stale1025b/repro_<ID>/). CURRENT, refs drifted; the guard is still absent and the contradiction is LIVE in an eighth shape: an unbound/UFCS call with no construct stamp into a method-only module. Rust `std::io::Write::write_all(out, b\"hello\\n\")`: io-boundaries classifies it fs_write std::io::Write.write_all, while verify-claims (generic claims) reports std::io::Write 'structurally invisible' on 7/7 claims (exit 2). Python `csv.DictWriter.writerow(w,row)` does the same once the language has any stamped edge. Cause: construct None -> reached_row_kind None -> route 1 fails; route 2 indexes function-kind names only. test_blind_language_method_starvation.py:523 (test_a_METHOD_name_on_an_unstamped_edge_still_starves) pins this on the premise 'an unstamped method-name edge is the blind-analyzer shape', which UFCS/unbound calls falsify; this is also ADR-0059's own re-open trigger (a row reached both ways). Instances 6-7 (JS assignment, python protocol) were fixed by WI-dapap c8754df23d -- the 'NOT merged' entry is stale. Refs: method_starved_modules verify_claims.py:4764 (crosswalk :4901); compute_boundary_coverage :4931 -> _call_production_coverage, starvation reason :5209-5224; call_constructs.py:164; io_boundary.classify_call :5580. Correction to option (b): it must live in _call_production_coverage or method_starved_modules, NOT compute_boundary_coverage -- claims_coverage_guard.coverage_of calls _call_production_coverage directly. Related: INV-pimir (now satisfied), WI-pukip (rust construct stamping). P3 kept; raise to P2 if a corpus count of UFCS calls into method-only modules is nonzero."  # 5ad0
